  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 255 AM EDT Wednesday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Isolated showers and storms are possible today, with \nmainly dry weather to end the week. Temperatures drop to slightly \nbelow average late this week.\n\nEarly morning wx analysis shows an anomalously strong low pressure \nsystem at the surface and aloft that continues to strengthen as it \ntracks along the Northeast CONUS coast. The associated trailing cold \nfront is crossing the area at this hour, with light NW winds and \nslightly lower dew pts across NW portions of the FA. Convection has \nended. Slightly below average temperatures and mostly dry wx is \nexpected from today through Friday as that low pressure system very \nslowly tracks from NY/NJ to northern New England. The cold front \nwill move to our SE later today...with 60s dew pts arriving in all \nareas except far SE VA and NE NC. Highs will generally be in the mid \n80s with partly to mostly cloudy skies due to cumulus given the \nclose proximity to the upper low. While most areas will stay dry, an \nisolated shower/tstm is possible from mid aftn through the evening, \nwith the best chance across the SE where dew pts (and thus \ninstability) will be highest. Will have no higher than 20% PoPs and \nhave noted that the blended guidance has no PoPs at all for today. \nThursday through Friday looks mostly dry as the low pressure system \nmoves farther away, with near to slightly below average \ntemperatures, as LLVL flow will continue to be out of the NW. \nOverall, quite pleasant for late July. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A typical summertime pattern returns by late this \nweekend and early next week, with near average temperatures and \nisolated-scattered diurnally driven convection each day.\n\nUpper heights gradually build from Friday-Saturday with temps \nwarming back up to near average and mostly dry wx continuing. A \nweaker trough (more typical of summertime) establishes itself over \nthe eastern CONUS late this weekend into early next week. \nAdditionally, dew pts rise and deep layer moisture increases during \nthis time. This will allow for daily tstm chances to return by Sunday \nand continue through at least Tuesday. Widespread severe wx is not \nexpected and temps remain around average.",
